  "term": "tonic",
  "definition": "In this source, tonic refers to a sustained pattern of nerve firing produced by repeated 4 Hz stimulation, in contrast to a brief burst-like phasic response at 1 Hz. It describes ongoing action potential activity during continuous or repetitive stimulation.",
